# Netlify SPA fallback.
#
# BrowserRouter puts real paths in the URL (/projects, /contact). Those
# paths don't exist as files on disk, so without this rule Netlify returns
# its own 404 for anyone who deep-links or hits refresh on one — the app
# would only ever work if you entered through "/".
#
# 200, not 301: serve index.html *at the requested URL* rather than
# redirecting to "/", so the router still sees the path the user asked for.
/*  /index.html  200
